{
  "dom_id": "step-e7959",
  "name": "Example: Working With Systems Containing Strict Inequalities",
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996965/assets/c9209c8978b86043b5d57d4a357a480a0209914598a0d7f2a810539cc050c473.png)\n\nWhich system of inequalities defines the shaded region shown above?",
  "worked_solution": "Consider the line $y=2x-3.$ Since the line is dashed, the inequality is strict. Also, since the shaded region lies *above* the line, the inequality is a \"greater than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny \\gt 2x - 3.\n$$\n\n    \n\nNow consider the line $y = x + 1.$ Since the line is dashed, the inequality is strict. Also, since the shaded region lies *below* the line, the inequality is a \"less than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny \\lt x+1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the system of inequalities that defines the shaded region is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}y>2x-3 \\\\ y<x+1.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "result": null,
